Method Path Who What it does GET <code>/api/rooms</code> student Rooms in hostels the student may live in, each with <code>is_own</code> and <code>open_to_swap</code> (how many occupants there want to swap). GET <code>/api/me/dashboard</code> student Current room, active request, swap chain (if any), progress steps and activity. POST <code>/api/requests</code> student Submit a ranked request (1–5 choices, best first). Returns <code>201 {tracking_id, status}</code>. See the body shapes below. DELETE <code>/api/requests/current</code> student Withdraw the active request (only while it is <code>open</code>). POST <code>/api/cycles/{id}/accept</code> student Confirm your place in a proposed chain. POST <code>/api/cycles/{id}/decline</code> student Decline: the chain is cancelled; you are withdrawn and the others go back to the pool. <p><code>POST /api/requests</code> accepts either shape:</p> <pre><code>{"room_ids": [12, 7]}
</code></pre> <pre><code>{"choices": [
  {"room_id": 12},
  {"type": {"hostel": "M", "seater": 1, "ac": true, "floor": 2}}
]}
</code></pre> <p>A <code>type</code> choice means "any room like this": a hostel code plus any of <code>seater</code> (1, 2 or 3 beds), <code>ac</code> (true / false) and <code>floor</code>. A filter left out means "any". Each choice gives either <code>room_id</code> or <code>type</code>, never both.</p>
